course: dictionary
lesson: 12996
title: Exploration
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Exploration is a noun, and it comes from the verb explore. To explore is to travel and look around a place to find out what is there. So exploration is the act of doing that: a trip or a search to discover something new.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The explorers sailed across the ocean to map new islands.» Sailing across the ocean and mapping islands tells you that exploration means finding out about places nobody knows well.
explain: The word also works for ideas. «Her exploration of the question took all afternoon.» Nobody sailed anywhere, so exploration must mean looking closely at a question to learn more.
explain: Medicine has its own meaning. Here the clues are words like doctor, hospital or check, not ships or maps. When you see one of these, the meaning changes to a doctor examining part of the body.
fact: Exploration is a noun. The verb is explore, and an explorer is a person who explores.
fact: «Exploration» means travelling to and looking around a place to find out what is there.
fact: «Exploration» can also mean looking closely at an idea or question to learn more.
fact: In medicine, «exploration» means a doctor examining part of the body.
fact: You will meet phrases like space exploration, ocean exploration and voyage of exploration.
exercise: «The team's exploration of the cave took three days.» What does exploration mean here? | *Travelling to and looking around the cave to find out what is there | Closing the cave for ever | Sleeping in the cave for three days | Painting pictures of the cave
exercise: «Her exploration of the question took all afternoon.» What does exploration mean here? | Writing the question on the board | Throwing the question away | *Looking closely at the question to learn more
exercise: Which word names the person who explores? | *explorer | exploring | explore
test: «The space exploration team sent a robot to Mars.» What does space exploration mean in this sentence? | *Finding out about faraway planets by travelling to them | Cleaning a spaceship | Watching films about stars
test: «The doctor's exploration showed the problem was in the knee.» What does exploration mean in this sentence? | A long trip to a new country | A quiz about the body | *A doctor examining part of the body
exam: Which meaning of exploration is correct? | Getting lost on purpose | Keeping a place clean and tidy | *Travelling to and looking around a place to find out what is there | Singing a song about a place
